{
  "rules": [
    "Strong upward-trend underestimation: in sustained rallies the model sits ~5–15 EUR below realized prices, with the gap widening with horizon (small at days 1–3, large by days 10–30). Apply an increasing positive bias with lead time.",
    "Trend/acceleration lag: the model reacts too slowly to upside momentum (misses step-changes). Use a momentum/acceleration term (e.g., recent 5–10d slope) to lift the whole path when the last 1–2 weeks are rising.",
    "Level anchoring/mean-reversion bias: forecasts revert toward ~68–71 even when the market transitions to a higher regime (~75–83). Add a regime-shift rule: if price breaks above recent range/highs, shift the forecast baseline upward rather than reverting.",
    "Horizon-specific correction: apply mild adjustment for days 1–5, moderate for days 6–15, and strongest for days 16–30 (because long-horizon errors dominate).",
    "Volatility/spike underpricing: during sharp upward moves the model underestimates peak magnitude and persistence. Inflate projected peaks and slow the decay after a breakout (reduce mean reversion strength following new highs)."
  ]
}
